.TH LLITE.OPEN_CACHE_STATS 4 2026-09-30 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
llite.open_cache_stats \- client open cache statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param llite." INSTANCE .open_cache_stats
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param llite." INSTANCE .open_cache_stats=clear
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per client mountpoint
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present on client
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR open_cache_stats (4)
parameter shows how effective the open cache is for a client mountpoint.
When the client holds an MDS open lock on a file,
the open handle is kept after the file is closed,
and later opens of the file reuse that handle without an RPC to the MDS.
The client requests the open lock with an open RPC once the file is opened
.B llite.*.opencache_threshold_count
times, or if it is reopened within
.B llite.*.opencache_threshold_ms
milliseconds of the last close.
.PP
Each counter is printed in the usual Lustre stats format,
with the counter name and the number of events since the
.B start_time
of the statistics.
Counters that are zero are not printed.
The counters are:
.TP
.B hits
The file open used an existing open handle on the client,
and no open RPC was sent to the MDS.
The open handle is either kept under a cached open lock,
or is in use by another open of the same file on this client.
.TP
.B misses
The file open needed an open RPC to the MDS.
.TP
.B threshold_count_locks
The open RPC requested an open lock, because the file was opened at least
.B opencache_threshold_count
times.
.TP
.B threshold_ms_locks
The open RPC requested an open lock, because the file was reopened within
.B opencache_threshold_ms
milliseconds of the last close.
.TP
.B miss_reopen_time
The time in milliseconds from the last close of the file to a reopen
that needed an open RPC because the client had no open handle for the file.
The minimum, maximum, and sum of the times are printed after the units.
The first open of a file on the client has no last close and is not included,
so there can be fewer samples than
.BR misses .
.PP
The fraction of
.B hits
out of all opens
.RB ( hits
plus
.BR misses )
is the share of opens that did not need an RPC to the MDS.
If there are many
.B misses
but few open locks are requested,
the thresholds are not being reached by the workload and
.B opencache_threshold_count
could be reduced, or
.B opencache_threshold_ms
could be increased.
.PP
The distribution of
.B miss_reopen_time
is shown by
.BR llite.open_cache_reopen_hist (4).
.PP
Writing any value to
.B open_cache_stats
resets all of the counters, and the
.BR llite.open_cache_reopen_hist (4)
histogram, to zero.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B llite.*.open_cache_stats
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the open cache statistics for all mountpoints on the local client:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl get_param llite.*.open_cache_stats"
llite.testfs-ffff888150068000.open_cache_stats=
snapshot_time                       1790789687.052634017 secs.nsecs
start_time                          1790789686.511679375 secs.nsecs
elapsed_time                        0.540954642 secs.nsecs
hits                                2 samples [reqs]
misses                              1 samples [reqs]
threshold_count_locks               1 samples [reqs]
miss_reopen_time                    1 samples [msecs] 12 12 12
.EE
.PP
Reset the open cache statistics for the
.B testfs
filesystem on the local client:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param llite.testfs-*.open_cache_stats=clear"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llite.*.open_cache_stats
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_59
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llite.open_cache_reopen_hist (4),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
